{"repositoryId":117079885,"availability":"available","full":"asterics/asterics-camerainput-cameramouse","name":"asterics-camerainput-cameramouse","description":"This folder contains a solution for a camera mouse enabling mouse control (moving mouse cursor, clicking and dragging) by head movements.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":8,"forks":0,"created":"2018-01-11T09:38:07Z","updated":"2021-05-04T06:40:46Z","branch":"master","homepage":"http://asterics.github.io/AsTeRICS/demos.html#xfacetrackerlk","topics":["accessibility","ape","assistive-technology","at-solution","camera","demo","example","face-tracking","head-tracking","mouse-emulation","webcam"],"demo":"http://asterics.github.io/AsTeRICS/demos.html#xfacetrackerlk","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T09:34:41.304Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T09:34:41.304Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T09:34:41.304Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T09:34:41.304Z","stars":8,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This folder contains a solution for a camera mouse enabling mouse control (moving mouse cursor, clicking and dragging) by head movements.","By moving the head up/down or left/right the mouse cursor should move accordingly. A left click is performed by dwelling (stopping movement and waiting for some time). To do a right, double or drag click select the respective button in the ARE GUI and move the cursor to the location where the click should be performed at. The mouse speed can be changed by using the slider. Click on the On/Off button to toggle mouse control.","The repository is an AsTeRICS based solution using the APE (AsTeRICS Packaging Environment)) template folder structure."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/asterics/asterics-camerainput-cameramouse/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"ae571d5caeb99a1d7e7a6d5ffd5f92f45b4e908c2bf39ec3b8fd38406590c227","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T09:34:41.445Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"202